---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Contact DevSnap — Report a Bug or Request a Tool"
  description="Get in touch with the DevSnap team. Report a wrong answer from a tool, request a tool you need, or say hello."
  schemas={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Contact DevSnap — Report a Bug or Request a Tool',
    url: `${SITE.domain}/contact/`,
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.publisher },
  }}
  canonicalPath="/contact/"
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    <ol class="crumbs">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li>Contact</li>
    </ol>

    <header class="tool-hero">
      <h1>Get in touch</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Bug reports, missing tools, corrections and "this saved me twenty minutes"
        messages are all welcome.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-3">
      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a monitored address, and a real person reads it. It is the fastest
        route to us and the only one we guarantee to answer.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting a wrong answer</h2>
      <p>
        A wrong answer from one of these tools is more important to us than a feature
        request, because a tool that gives a confident wrong result breaks somebody's
        build and they will not know why. If you send one, include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The tool you were using and the URL of its page.</li>
        <li>The input that produced the wrong result.</li>
        <li>What you expected and what you got instead.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You do not need to scrub the input before sending it — but please do scrub
        anything that is a live credential. The tools run locally precisely so that a
        secret never has to leave your machine, and a bug report is an exception you
        can avoid.
      </p>

      <h2>Requesting a tool</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us what you were trying to do, not just what you want built. The best
        requests we have received described a moment of friction — "I need to convert
        this payload into a form body and then check it against a schema" — and the
        tool that came out of it was more useful than the one that would have come
        from a feature list.
      </p>

      <h2>Response time</h2>
      <p>
        Usually within a few working days. A report that describes a wrong answer is
        prioritised over a feature request, and a request that blocks your work is
        prioritised over both.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
